{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 23,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even to-day is my complaint rebellious:\nMy stroke is heavier than my groaning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that I knew where I might find him!\nThat I might come even to his seat!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would set my cause in order before him,\nAnd fill my mouth with arguments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would know the words which he would answer me,\nAnd understand what he would say unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Would he contend with me in the greatness of his power?\nNay; but he would give heed unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There the upright might reason with him;\nSo should I be delivered for ever from my judge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I go forward, but he is not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";\nAnd backward, but I cannot perceive him;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "On the left hand, when he doth work, but I cannot behold him;\nHe hideth himself on the right hand, that I cannot see him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he knoweth the way that I take;\nWhen he hath tried me, I shall come forth as gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My foot hath held fast to his steps;\nHis way have I kept, and turned not aside.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have not gone back from the commandment of his lips;\nI have treasured up the words of his mouth more than my necessary food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he is in one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mind",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and who can turn him?\nAnd what his soul desireth, even that he doeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he performeth that which is appointed for me:\nAnd many such things are with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore am I terrified at his presence;\nWhen I consider, I am afraid of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For God hath made my heart faint,\nAnd the Almighty hath terrified me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.23.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.23.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because I was not cut off before the darkness,\nNeither did he cover the thick darkness from my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
